# 6. DECISION-MAKING LOGIC

The intended security behaviour is:

| Voice verification | Second-device approval | System decision |
|---|---|---|
| Pass | Valid authorised approval | Permit simulated action |
| Pass | Pending | Keep request locked |
| Pass | Rejected | Block action |
| Borderline | Pending peer review | Keep request locked |
| Borderline | Approved after required review | Permit according to policy |
| Fail | Any approval attempt | Block action |
| Any result | Expired approval | Reject approval |
| Any result | Reused approval | Reject approval |

**Important:** A second-device approval must not override a hard voice-verification failure. A failed verification remains blocked. Borderline results require additional review rather than automatic acceptance.

The actual numerical thresholds for Pass, Borderline and Fail must be determined from DetectifAI's documented response fields and testing. They must not be invented or assumed.

